// ADR-0009 / ADR-0012: query keys must come from a feature's key factory.
//
// An inline key that differs from the factory's by one segment creates a
// second cache entry that SSE updates never reach. The symptom appears months
// later as a view that silently stopped refreshing, with nothing to point at.
// This is the guardrail that makes ADR-0009's central invariant enforceable
// rather than merely remembered.
//
// It needs no path exemption: key factories declare arrays under their own
// property names (`all:`, `detail:`), not under `queryKey:`, so this pattern
// does not match them.
//
// Verified to fire on `queryKey: ['jobs']` and not on
// `queryKey: jobsKeys.lists()`.
language js

`queryKey: $key` where {
  $key <: `[$...]`,
  register_diagnostic(span=$key, message="Inline query key. Use the feature's key factory from features/*/api — an inline key creates a cache entry SSE updates will never reach (ADR-0009).", severity="error")
}
